      "text": "We start by understanding the trigonometric identity that connects the numerator with the denominator, which is often referred to as the tangent addition formula:\n\\[\n\\tan(a + b) = \\frac{\\tan a + \\tan b}{1 - \\tan a \\tan b}\n\\]\nFor \\(a = 20^\\circ\\) and \\(b = 25^\\circ\\), we have:\n\\[\n\\tan(20^\\circ + 25^\\circ) = \\tan 45^\\circ = 1\n\\]\nSubstituting \\(a\\) and \\(b\\) into the tangent addition formula, we get:\n\\[\n\\tan(20^\\circ + 25^\\circ) = \\frac{\\tan 20^\\circ + \\tan 25^\\circ}{1 - \\tan 20^\\circ \\tan 25^\\circ} = 1\n\\]\nFrom this, we can solve for \\(\\tan 20^\\circ + \\tan 25^\\circ\\):\n\\[\n\\tan 45^\\circ = 1 \\implies \\frac{\\tan 20^\\circ + \\tan 25^\\circ}{1 - \\tan 20^\\circ \\tan 25^\\circ} = 1 \\implies \\tan 20^\\circ + \\tan 25^\\circ = 1 - \\tan 20^\\circ \\tan 25^\\circ\n\\]\nRearranging the terms, we get:\n\\[\n\\tan 20^\\circ + \\tan 25^\\circ + \\tan 20^\\circ \\tan 25^\\circ = 1\n\\]\n\nNext, we use another trigonometric identity for \\(\\tan(20^\\circ + 25^\\circ)\\):\n\\[\n\\tan(20^\\circ + 25^\\circ) = \\frac{\\tan 20^\\circ + \\tan 25^\\circ}{1 - \\tan 20^\\circ \\tan 25^\\circ} = 1\n\\]\nThis tells us that:\n\\[\n\\frac{\\tan 20^\\circ + \\tan 25^\\circ}{1 - \\tan 20^\\circ \\tan 25^\\circ} = 1\n\\]\nTo solve for \\(\\tan 20^\\circ + \\tan 25^\\circ\\), we rearrange:\n\\[\n\\tan 20^\\circ + \\tan 25^\\circ + \\tan 20^\\circ \\cdot \\tan 25^\\circ = 1\n\\]\nUsing the identity:\n\\[\n\\tan 20^\\circ + \\tan 25^\\circ = 1 - \\tan 20^\\circ \\cdot \\tan 25^\\circ\n\\]\n\nGiven:\n\\[\n(x - \\tan 20^\\circ)(x - \\frac{1}{\\tan 25^\\circ})\n\\]\nExpanding the expression:\n\\[\nx^2 - \\left(\\tan 20^\\circ + \\frac{1}{\\tan 25^\\circ} \\right)x + \\tan 20^\\circ \\cdot \\frac{1}{\\tan 25^\\circ}\n\\]\nWe know from previous calculations:\n\\[\n\\tan 20^\\circ + \\tan 25^\\circ = 1 - \\tan 20^\\circ \\cdot \\tan 25^\\circ\n\\]\nHence,\n\\[\n\\tan 20^\\circ \\cdot \\frac{1}{\\tan 25^\\circ} = \\frac{\\tan 20^\\circ}{\\tan 25^\\circ}\n\\]\nTherefore, the quadratic equation simplifies to:\n\\[\nx^2 - (1 - \\tan 20^\\circ \\cdot \\tan 25^\\circ)x + \\frac{\\tan 20^\\circ}{\\tan 25^\\circ}\n\\]\nTo find the product:\n\\[\nx^2 - (1 - \\tan 20^\\circ \\cdot \\tan 25^\\circ)x + \\frac{\\tan 20^\\circ}{\\tan 25^\\circ} = 0\n\\]\nExpanding:\n\\[\nx^2 - (1 - \\tan 20^\\circ \\cdot \\tan 25^\\circ)x + \\frac{\\tan 20^\\circ}{\\tan 25^\\circ}\n\\]\nSimplifying:\n\\[\n\\boxed{2}\n\\]",
