      "sample_index": 1,
      "text": "To simplify \\((1 + \\tan 20^\\circ)(1 + \\tan 25^\\circ)\\), we start by using the tangent addition formula. The formula for the tangent of the sum of two angles is:\n\n\\[\n\\tan (a + b) = \\frac{\\tan a + \\tan b}{1 - \\tan a \\tan b}\n\\]\n\nLet's set \\(a = 20^\\circ\\) and \\(b = 25^\\circ\\). Then we have:\n\n\\[\n\\tan (20^\\circ + 25^\\circ) = \\tan 45^\\circ = 1\n\\]\n\nUsing the tangent addition formula, we get:\n\n\\[\n\\tan 45^\\circ = \\frac{\\tan 20^\\circ + \\tan 25^\\circ}{1 - \\tan 20^\\circ \\tan 25^\\circ} = 1\n\\]\n\nThis equation can be rewritten as:\n\n\\[\n\\tan 20^\\circ + \\tan 25^\\circ = 1 - \\tan 20^\\circ \\tan 25^\\circ\n\\]\n\nNow, we multiply both sides of this equation by \\(1 + \\tan 20^\\circ \\tan 25^\\circ\\):\n\n\\[\n(\\tan 20^\\circ + \\tan 25^\\circ)(1 + \\tan 20^\\circ \\tan 25^\\circ) = (1 - \\tan 20^\\circ \\tan 25^\\circ)(1 + \\tan 20^\\circ \\tan 25^\\circ)\n\\]\n\nThe right-hand side simplifies using the difference of squares:\n\n\\[\n(1 - \\tan 20^\\circ \\tan 25^\\circ)(1 + \\tan 20^\\circ \\tan 25^\\circ) = 1 - (\\tan 20^\\circ \\tan 25^\\circ)^2\n\\]\n\nSo the equation becomes:\n\n\\[\n(\\tan 20^\\circ + \\tan 25^\\circ)(1 + \\tan 20^\\circ \\tan 25^\\circ) = 1 - (\\tan 20^\\circ \\tan 25^\\circ)^2\n\\]\n\nNotice that the left-hand side expands to:\n\n\\[\n\\tan 20^\\circ + \\tan 25^\\circ + \\tan 20^\\circ \\tan 25^\\circ + (\\tan 20^\\circ \\tan 25^\\circ)^2\n\\]\n\nAnd the right-hand side is:\n\n\\[\n1 - (\\tan 20^\\circ \\tan 25^\\circ)^2\n\\]\n\nTherefore, we have:\n\n\\[\n\\tan 20^\\circ + \\tan 25^\\circ + \\tan 20^\\circ \\tan 25^\\circ + (\\tan 20^\\circ \\tan 25^\\circ)^2 = 1 - (\\tan 20^\\circ \\tan 25^\\circ)^2\n\\]\n\nLet \\(x = \\tan 20^\\circ \\tan 25^\\circ\\). Then the equation becomes:\n\n\\[\n\\tan 20^\\circ + \\tan 25^\\circ + x + x^2 = 1 - x^2\n\\]\n\nCombining like terms, we get:\n\n\\[\n\\tan 20^\\circ + \\tan 25^\\circ + 2x^2 + x = 1\n\\]\n\nAdding 1 to both sides, we have:\n\n\\[\n\\tan 20^\\circ + \\tan 25^\\circ + 2x^2 + x + 1 = 2\n\\]\n\nNotice that:\n\n\\[\n\\tan 20^\\circ + \\tan 25^\\circ + (x + 1)^2 = 2\n\\]\n\nThis implies:\n\n\\[\n\\tan 20^\\circ + \\tan 25^\\circ + (x + 1)^2 = 2\n\\]\n\nSince \\(x = \\tan 20^\\circ \\tan 25^\\circ\\) and we know from the tangent addition formula that:\n\n\\[\n\\tan 45^\\circ = 1 = \\frac{\\tan 20^\\circ + \\tan 25^\\circ}{1 - \\tan 20^\\circ \\tan 25^\\circ}\n\\]\n\nWe can simplify our equation to:\n\n\\[\n(\\tan 20^\\circ + \\tan 25^\\circ)(1 + \\tan 20^\\circ \\tan 25^\\circ) = 1 - \\tan 20^\\circ \\tan 25^\\circ\n\\]\n\nThis simplifies to:\n\n\\[\n\\frac{\\tan 20^\\circ + \\tan 25^\\circ}{1 - \\tan 20^\\circ \\tan 25^\\circ} = 1\n\\]\n\nSo we get:\n\n\\[\n(\\tan 20^\\circ + \\tan 25^\\circ)(1 + \\tan 20^\\circ \\tan 25^\\circ) = 1 - \\tan 20^\\circ \\tan 25^\\circ\n\\]\n\nThus, we have:\n\n\\[\n\\boxed{2}\n\\]",
